WEBVTT

00:01.100 --> 00:04.937
"It seems today that all you see

00:05.062 --> 00:08.398
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:08.398 --> 00:12.027
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:12.152 --> 00:15.154
"On which we used to rely?

00:15.279 --> 00:18.407
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:18.490 --> 00:23.286
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:23.411 --> 00:25.080
"Laugh and cry

00:25.163 --> 00:30.293
"He's a family guy

00:35.298 --> 00:38.926
- Hi, Chris.
- Hi, Barbara.

00:39.051 --> 00:42.261
I'm having a birthday party.
I was hoping you could come.

00:42.386 --> 00:45.597
Oh, no! Someone peed in my pants!

00:46.974 --> 00:49.977
You're funny. Well, I hope you can make it.

00:52.062 --> 00:54.689
Your friend's party sounds like fun, Chris.

00:54.772 --> 00:58.234
But I hope the cake's better
than the last party I went to.

01:00.820 --> 01:03.447
Oh, God. Coconut.

01:03.447 --> 01:08.450
I wanna get Barbara a really nice gift. What
kind of gifts have boys gotten for you, Meg?

01:08.534 --> 01:09.995
Oh... well...

01:10.120 --> 01:13.539
My boyfriend Prince William
got me this beautiful watch.

01:13.664 --> 01:16.875
And this diamond tiara.
And this wonderful sceptre.

01:22.923 --> 01:26.050
She needs to get laid, big-time.

01:26.176 --> 01:29.929
I read a book saying women are from Venus,
so here's what you get her.

01:30.012 --> 01:32.723
Layers of sulphuric acid,
viscous surface rock,

01:32.848 --> 01:37.310
and coronae, which seem to be domes over
large magma chambers. Here's five dollars.

01:37.435 --> 01:42.939
That's OK, Dad. I was thinking about getting
a paper route so I could buy her gift myself.

01:43.064 --> 01:45.442
I think that's very sweet, honey.

01:45.567 --> 01:49.113
Oh, boy. I remember my first job.
I was in a folk music trio.

01:49.196 --> 01:52.115
Hey, how about
"Here's To You, Mrs Fleckenstein"?

01:52.241 --> 01:55.577
You've been pitching that for an hour.
It's not an attractive name.

01:55.660 --> 01:56.912
Oh, fine.

01:57.037 --> 01:58.995
I suppose we're also not going with

01:59.120 --> 02:02.457
"Parsley, Sage,
Rosemary and Lawry's Seasoning Salt".

02:02.541 --> 02:04.125
That's it. I'm going to Nam.

02:08.921 --> 02:12.883
Hey, there, young fella.
Bringin' me good news today?

02:12.967 --> 02:15.261
- What?
- Come on over here, son.

02:15.386 --> 02:18.180
Hand me the paper,
so I don't need to use my grabber.

02:18.305 --> 02:19.765
Mm.

02:19.848 --> 02:23.519
- That's a nice muscly throwin' arm you got.
- Uh, thanks.

02:23.602 --> 02:27.772
Got a nice tip for you right here
in my pocket, but my arthritis...

02:27.897 --> 02:30.690
Why don't you reach in
and fish it out for yourself?

02:30.815 --> 02:34.361
That's OK, mister.
I don't collect till the end of the month.

02:34.444 --> 02:36.947
I'll see you tomorrow. Weird.

02:40.491 --> 02:45.204
- I hope you like it.
- Wow, perfume. That is so sweet.

02:45.288 --> 02:50.626
It'll make you smell like Elizabeth Taylor. So
I guess you'll smell of bourbon and Vicodin.

02:50.626 --> 02:53.419
- That's very thoughtful.
- Can I spray some on you?

02:53.544 --> 02:56.129
- Ow! My eyes!
- They're beautiful.

02:56.254 --> 02:58.841
Just get away from me, Chris!

02:58.966 --> 03:01.969
I'm so awkward!

03:04.888 --> 03:07.932
Hey, muscly-arm. Why the long face?

03:08.016 --> 03:13.645
It's this girl. I can't talk to her. It's like
girls are a different species or somethin'.

03:13.770 --> 03:17.941
- Aw, who needs 'em? You like Popsicles?
- Well, sure.

03:18.024 --> 03:24.280
Then you need to come on down to the cellar.
I got a whole freezer full of Popsicles. Mm.

03:24.405 --> 03:26.698
No, thanks. I gotta get goin'.

03:26.782 --> 03:29.201
Don't make me beg, now.

03:29.285 --> 03:32.411
You're funny. Bye.

03:32.538 --> 03:34.623
Get your fat ass back here.

03:39.836 --> 03:43.797
- This is a hold-up. Open the register.
- It only opens when you make a sale.

03:43.880 --> 03:48.259
All right, then give me one of them
horoscope scrolls and some Skittles.

03:48.384 --> 03:52.138
"Financial transaction
benefits you today. " Oooh!

03:52.221 --> 03:54.432
Weird!

04:00.688 --> 04:03.607
All right! A bike! I'm outta here.

04:08.278 --> 04:14.449
Your parents are on their way, but since time
is a factor here we'd like to get an ID quickly.

04:15.908 --> 04:20.079
- Are you sure he can't see me?
- Absolutely, Chris. You're 100% safe.

04:20.162 --> 04:22.790
OK. That's him. Number six.

04:22.790 --> 04:27.044
Hi. Excuse me, you guys.
I'm here to pick up my son, Chris Griffin.

04:27.169 --> 04:32.674
He's here to finger the guy who held up that
store. Maybe you've seen him. Chris Griffin.

04:32.799 --> 04:36.135
Wait a second, I got a picture of him
somewhere. Here you go.

04:36.218 --> 04:40.513
Hang on to that, I got a ton of 'em at home.
I was gonna throw that one out anyway.

04:40.598 --> 04:45.601
Chris messed it up by writing his school
schedule and a list of his fears on the back.

04:48.521 --> 04:52.692
We're so proud of you, Chris,
for helping to put that horrible man in jail.

04:52.817 --> 04:55.320
You couldn't have said
it was Cйline Dion, huh?

04:55.404 --> 04:59.573
Our chance to put that showboating
Canadian wench behind bars and you blow it.

04:59.699 --> 05:03.659
We now return
to the "E! True Hollywood Story: ALF".

05:03.742 --> 05:08.038
By the third season
I was completely wasted all the time.

05:08.121 --> 05:10.624
I'd lost all control of my bodily functions.

05:10.749 --> 05:14.170
They had to cut the crap out of my fur
before each taping.

05:14.295 --> 05:16.462
But, uh, would I do it all again?

05:16.588 --> 05:19.299
We interrupt this programme
for a news story.

05:19.383 --> 05:25.554
Now over to Rhode Island State Penitentiary
and Asian reporter Tricia Takanawa. Tricia?

05:25.554 --> 05:32.434
I'm at this maximum-security facility, where a
ruthless thug has engineered a daring escape.

05:32.518 --> 05:35.855
Sir, do you have any plans
now that you're out of jail?

05:35.980 --> 05:40.234
Yeah. I'm gonna go bang my girlfriend,
and then I'm gonna kill Chris Griffin!

05:40.359 --> 05:42.236
Good Lord!

05:42.236 --> 05:45.780
Can they really say
"bang my girlfriend" on TV?

05:49.742 --> 05:51.702
You wanna remove us from the area?

05:51.827 --> 05:57.249
This man will stop at nothing. We're placing
you all in the Witness Protection Program.

05:57.332 --> 06:01.836
Is Europe an option? I've always wanted
to spend a year in Prague teaching English.

06:01.920 --> 06:04.546
Slacking off,
but really getting to know myself.

06:04.630 --> 06:08.092
Until we catch this guy,
you'll be relocated to the Deep South.

06:08.175 --> 06:10.803
The Deep South?

06:10.886 --> 06:12.971
Where the black guys are really lazy,

06:13.096 --> 06:17.142
and the white guys are just as lazy but
they're mad at the black guys for being lazy?

06:17.267 --> 06:20.895
Jenkins and I have been assigned
to live here and watch your house.

06:21.019 --> 06:24.022
He's a slovenly liberal
and I'm a fastidious conservative.

06:24.147 --> 06:28.401
- I smell a sitcom!
- I suggest you start packing immediately.

06:31.447 --> 06:36.034
I can't believe I have to change schools
because of you. This is all your fault, Lardo.

06:36.117 --> 06:38.827
- Me? I had nothing to do with it.
- I meant Chris.

06:38.952 --> 06:41.122
Oh. Yeah, Lardo.

06:41.247 --> 06:45.001
Look, everybody. Here we are.
The town of Bumblescum.

06:53.215 --> 06:55.842
- This is our house?
- Come on, Meg.

06:55.926 --> 06:59.262
I bet if we fixed it up a little bit,
it could be a piece of crap.

07:03.350 --> 07:07.812
- What's that smell?
- It's either bad meat or good cheese.

07:08.855 --> 07:11.981
There's a penny underneath that couch.

07:12.398 --> 07:14.608
Somebody's in the closet!

07:14.608 --> 07:18.570
You know you're a redneck
when your gun rack has a gun rack on it.

07:18.654 --> 07:20.865
You suck!

07:22.949 --> 07:29.206
Oh, my. Well, it's too hot to cook anyway.
Peter, what's the upstairs like?

07:29.289 --> 07:31.291
There's a Crunch Berry under the fridge.

07:31.374 --> 07:34.919
Mom, Chris found a jar in the basement
and it has a hand in it.

07:35.044 --> 07:38.172
I'm gonna plant it and see if a human grows.

07:38.672 --> 07:42.550
Well, at least the TV gets decent reception.

07:42.634 --> 07:44.636
Must be some kind of nature show.

07:44.719 --> 07:47.347
Help! Help! Get it off! Aaargh!

07:47.763 --> 07:51.100
Great. We're here five minutes
and Dad gets mauled by a rodent.

07:51.100 --> 07:54.228
- This place is horrible.
- OK, everybody calm down.

07:54.312 --> 07:56.939
We don't know anything
about this community.

07:57.022 --> 08:00.901
I bet if we explore the town
we'll each find something about it we like.

08:00.984 --> 08:03.695
That's a great idea.
I just gotta hit the can.

08:03.820 --> 08:05.695
I think there's just an outhouse.

08:07.990 --> 08:11.618
Hey, Lois? I don't get how this works.
It's just a hole.

08:11.743 --> 08:14.037
I don't think it goes anywhere.

08:14.120 --> 08:16.414
No, it definitely doesn't go anywhere.

08:16.539 --> 08:18.291
Aaaargh!

08:18.416 --> 08:19.750
Oh, God!

08:19.875 --> 08:23.211
Oh, it's everywhere! Aaaaargh!

08:23.294 --> 08:27.591
It's in my raccoon wounds! Oh, God!

08:29.551 --> 08:33.221
- Excuse me, do you have an ATM?
- Over there, ma'am.

08:33.304 --> 08:35.722
- How much you wanna take out?
- 40 dollars.

08:35.806 --> 08:39.059
There's a service charge of a buck 50.
Do y'all accept?

08:39.142 --> 08:40.727
Yes.

08:40.811 --> 08:43.855
Mm. You smell like
the inside of my momma's purse.

08:43.938 --> 08:46.149
Thank you.

08:48.109 --> 08:52.905
What are those dulcet tones?
Why, this is the music of the angels!

08:53.030 --> 08:56.783
- What is that magical device?
- Banjo.

08:58.451 --> 09:00.953
Pluck that string.

09:01.037 --> 09:05.540
Oh, I feel so deliciously white-trash.
Mommy, I want a mullet!

09:06.875 --> 09:09.294
All right, that about does it.

09:09.378 --> 09:12.715
- Isn't she beautiful, Brian?
- The Duke boys would be proud.

09:12.840 --> 09:15.967
Yeah, and you gotta get in
through the window, like this.

09:16.050 --> 09:18.678
OK, now you.

09:18.678 --> 09:22.015
Oh, sorry. I forgot to roll yours down.

09:22.098 --> 09:24.724
You all right?

09:24.807 --> 09:26.476
Hello?

09:26.601 --> 09:28.770
Wake up, sleepyhead.

09:32.314 --> 09:34.525
- Hi.
- Hi.

09:35.025 --> 09:37.652
- Are you mad at that pond?
- Shoot, no.

09:37.735 --> 09:40.363
'Course, this pond did kill my grandpappy.

09:40.363 --> 09:44.951
He saw his reflection, thought it was him
and drowned trying to save himself.

09:45.035 --> 09:47.538
That's why Mom
doesn't let me look in the toilet.

09:47.663 --> 09:49.746
- I'm Sam.
- I'm Chris.

09:49.829 --> 09:51.624
Sam, come on in, now.

09:51.707 --> 09:57.878
Well, I gotta go help my daddy bring in the
mud harvest. Nice making your acquaintance.

09:58.296 --> 10:01.507
Oh, my God, I'm drowning!

10:02.675 --> 10:07.471
That was Merle Haggard with
"I Kissed My Sweetie With My Fist". Next...

10:07.554 --> 10:09.848
There's one. Let's jump that.

10:13.518 --> 10:16.436
Yeee-haaa!

10:18.522 --> 10:22.984
That was great! Next time, let's get Meg
to be Boss Hogg and Chris can be Anus.

10:23.109 --> 10:24.443
- Enos.
- What'd I say?

10:24.568 --> 10:26.237
Anus.

10:29.365 --> 10:31.534
Class, we have a new student joinin' us.

10:31.659 --> 10:35.622
Everyone, please welcome
Megan Griffin, from the North.

10:37.497 --> 10:40.417
What's it like there?
Y'all got them talkin' pictures?

10:40.417 --> 10:43.544
- And flyin' machines?
- And perfume for your armpits?

10:43.627 --> 10:46.338
- We sure do.
- Wow.

10:46.463 --> 10:51.259
All right, that's enough questions for Megan.
Time to hand back last week's spelling tests.

10:51.342 --> 10:54.596
- And it looks like Oinky's set the curve again.
- Dang.

10:54.596 --> 10:57.599
- That is some smart pig.
- Good thing I copied off Oinky.

10:59.684 --> 11:02.312
Ta-da! Possum surprise.

11:02.395 --> 11:04.897
Actually, I made it with Shake 'n Bake.

11:05.022 --> 11:07.732
- And I helped.
- Kids, where's your father?

11:07.815 --> 11:10.527
Yeee-haaa!

11:12.319 --> 11:16.490
- What the hell are you doing?!
- Blendin' in. Relax, Lois. It's not our house.

11:16.573 --> 11:21.161
I'm glad you're having fun, but we need
money. Have you thought about a job?

11:21.286 --> 11:25.456
Yes, Lois, I have. But I've also thought
about getting fired from that job.

11:25.540 --> 11:30.670
Is that something you wanna put our family
through? Think about that while I get a drink.

11:30.753 --> 11:33.255
Aaagh! Aaargh! Oh, God! Aaagh!

11:33.796 --> 11:36.508
It's right up here past this clearing.

11:36.591 --> 11:39.427
- He's been here about three months now.
- Wow.

11:39.510 --> 11:41.596
Where do you think you go when you die?

11:41.721 --> 11:44.723
I learned at church that
if you're good you go to heaven.

11:44.849 --> 11:48.811
If you're bad, you go to a place
where the dead believe they're still livin'

11:48.894 --> 11:52.230
and they pray for death,
but death won't come.

11:52.355 --> 11:54.650
UPN?

11:54.733 --> 11:58.820
- You're funny. I like you, Chris.
- I like you too, Sam.

11:58.902 --> 12:01.404
- Wanna poke him?
- Do I?!

12:02.989 --> 12:07.869
You know, it's true.
The best things in life really are free.

12:08.912 --> 12:12.665
I don't know. Maybe Lois is right.
Maybe it is time for me to get a job.

12:12.791 --> 12:14.875
You always blow it in the interview.

12:14.958 --> 12:17.878
So, Peter, where do you see yourself
in five years?

12:18.003 --> 12:20.714
Don't say "Doing your wife. "

12:20.798 --> 12:22.799
Doing your...

12:22.799 --> 12:25.176
son?

12:25.301 --> 12:27.678
Hey, Brian. Look at that.

12:27.803 --> 12:33.850
Y'all interested? We take turns being sheriff.
You just hang out here, eat pie and get drunk.

12:33.933 --> 12:38.230
Hold on a second. "Pie"? "Drunk"? "The"?

12:38.313 --> 12:40.314
You got yourself a sheriff!

12:41.357 --> 12:45.319
- Boy, it's so quiet around here.
- I know.

12:45.402 --> 12:48.113
The phone hasn't rung all day.

12:48.238 --> 12:52.074
I kn... I know. There's nothin'...
nothin' to, um...

12:53.034 --> 12:55.327
to, uh...

12:56.370 --> 12:58.455
um...

12:59.582 --> 13:02.292
uh... Oh, boy,
what's the word I'm looking for? Do.

13:02.417 --> 13:05.003
Brian, you're drunk. You're drunk.

13:05.128 --> 13:07.213
Give me your keys.

13:08.673 --> 13:11.801
- What is this, Dad?
- A Southern tradition, son.

13:11.884 --> 13:14.304
It's a re-enactment of the Civil War.

13:15.846 --> 13:22.518
Robert E Lee. I knew I'd find you here,
where they seat the sorry-ass losers.

13:22.643 --> 13:28.356
Ulysses S Grant, you invite me to lunch
then show up an hour late, drunk?

13:28.481 --> 13:33.278
I was busy lookin' for your wife,
to give her the old...

13:33.361 --> 13:36.197
Sir, this means war.

13:36.281 --> 13:37.657
I am vanquished.

13:37.740 --> 13:42.245
I hereby declare victory
in the name of the Confederacy.

13:45.371 --> 13:48.374
Excuse me. I don't think
that's how it happened.

13:48.499 --> 13:51.503
- I'm pretty sure the North won.
- What are you sayin'?

13:51.628 --> 13:56.007
That drunken idiot kicked your sorry asses
south of the Donna Dixon Line.

13:56.090 --> 13:58.717
We don't take kindly
to that sort of talk, mister.

13:58.800 --> 14:02.554
And I sure as shoot don't want
your kid hangin' round with my kid.

14:02.679 --> 14:08.392
And if you think I'm mad now, you gotta
answer to them Civil War survivors.

14:09.351 --> 14:14.773
Wait! Look over there! It's an interracial
gay couple burning the American flag!

14:16.858 --> 14:18.318
Get 'em!

14:21.320 --> 14:24.448
- I guess we can't hang out any more.
- I guess not.

14:24.573 --> 14:27.785
That sucks,
cos I really like spending time with you.

14:27.910 --> 14:29.994
Me too.

14:32.289 --> 14:34.374
What are you doing?

14:38.960 --> 14:44.174
Them Griffin boys better
grow some wings, or start flappin' their arms.

14:49.887 --> 14:51.889
- Lost 'em!
- Blasted Lincoln-lovers.

14:51.972 --> 14:53.349
Anyone seen my foot?

14:55.434 --> 15:02.524
Man, was last night weird. I kissed a boy! But
I really like him as a friend. His name is Sam.

15:02.607 --> 15:05.025
- You kissed Sam last night?
- How did you know?

15:05.109 --> 15:07.612
You said it out loud.
I heard you in the other room.

15:07.737 --> 15:11.156
The weird thing is,
kissing Sam kind of felt right.

15:11.281 --> 15:14.827
But I don't know if I can face him again.
Brian, what should I do?

15:14.910 --> 15:18.037
I haven't been this confused
since the end of No Way Out.

15:19.831 --> 15:23.167
How does Kevin Costner keep getting work?

15:26.920 --> 15:29.839
- Argh! How do I shoot? How do I shoot?
- Press B button.

15:31.925 --> 15:34.427
- Telegram for Chris Griffin.
- He's not here.

15:34.510 --> 15:37.013
- Where is he?
- I can't release that information.

15:37.138 --> 15:40.474
Oh, did I say Chris? I meant Chris's sister.

15:40.557 --> 15:45.271
Oh, well, if it's for Meg,
that's a whole other story. Here's her address.

15:45.354 --> 15:48.064
- What are you doing?
- You were busy. I played your guy.

15:48.189 --> 15:50.775
- I didn't wanna play.
- So it's good for everybody.

15:50.900 --> 15:54.110
- I'm gonna draw boobs on the Etch A Sketch.
- They'll end up square.

15:55.571 --> 15:58.199
- Oh, hi, Chris.
- Hey.

15:58.282 --> 16:01.742
Um, listen, Sam.
I like hangin' out with you and all,

16:01.825 --> 16:05.287
it's just that I don't want
a romantic relationship.

16:05.371 --> 16:10.167
- But I'd like it if we could still be friends.
- I'd like that too. Wanna go for a swim?

16:10.292 --> 16:12.169
Sure.

16:14.754 --> 16:17.674
- You're a girl?!
- Of course I am.

16:17.799 --> 16:19.552
Oh, my God!

16:23.846 --> 16:26.556
Warm out today.

16:26.556 --> 16:29.143
Warm yesterday.

16:29.267 --> 16:31.352
Even warmer today.

16:33.021 --> 16:36.148
"Met her on my CB, said her name was Mimi

16:36.148 --> 16:39.569
- " Sounded like an angel come to earth
- " Come to earth

16:39.694 --> 16:42.821
"When I went to meet her,
man, you should have seen her

16:42.821 --> 16:45.824
- " Twice as tall as me, three times the girth
- " Girth

16:45.948 --> 16:49.576
- " Oh, my fat baby loves to eat
- " Loves to eat

16:49.701 --> 16:53.038
"A big old Buddha belly
and her breasts swing past her feet

16:53.038 --> 16:56.166
"My fat baby loves to eat

16:56.249 --> 16:59.587
"My big ole fat-ass baby loves to eat

17:00.628 --> 17:03.339
I got blisters on my fingers!

17:05.008 --> 17:08.677
- A drop more of the shine, my dear?
- Yes, please.

17:08.677 --> 17:12.097
You know, the kids are gonna be
at that town social for a while.

17:12.222 --> 17:15.140
I think I know where you're going.

17:16.893 --> 17:19.394
Aaagh! Aaagh! Oh, God! Aaagh! Aaagh!

17:19.519 --> 17:21.480
Hello?

17:21.605 --> 17:25.151
Hello, Mrs Griffin? Yeah.
Shh! Shut up! You guys, shut up!

17:25.234 --> 17:27.944
Yeah, this is the FBI, calling from your house.

17:28.069 --> 17:30.447
Oh, hi. How is everything?

17:30.572 --> 17:32.448
Good, good. Real good.

17:32.531 --> 17:37.244
Listen, promise you won't be mad,
and it's probably nothing,

17:37.244 --> 17:43.291
but you know that criminal who's after your
son? He might know where you guys are.

17:43.374 --> 17:48.087
What?! Peter, that criminal is on his way here
to kill Chris. We gotta call the sheriff.

17:48.170 --> 17:51.423
Holy crap. I'm on it, Lois.

17:51.507 --> 17:57.137
Sheriff's office. Yes, this is Peter Griffin. I'd
like to report a criminal coming into town.

17:57.262 --> 18:02.141
I'm sorry, could you repeat your name?
Yes, it's Peter Griffin. G-r-i-f-f-i-n.

18:02.267 --> 18:05.269
- You're the sheriff?
- One sec, honey. I'm on the phone.

18:05.394 --> 18:08.522
- Who's that? My wife.
- Peter, Chris is in danger!

18:08.522 --> 18:10.690
Do something! Round up a posse.

18:10.815 --> 18:15.820
Yeah, well, see, I kinda pissed off the whole
town at that Civil War re-enactment.

18:15.903 --> 18:18.531
- What are we gonna do?
- I don't know, Lois.

18:18.615 --> 18:21.534
But I feel lower than a bow-legged caterpillar.

18:21.659 --> 18:24.161
Now here's Roy.

18:28.540 --> 18:32.292
- Sure is a ding-dang of a hoedown.
- Uh-uh. This here's a hootenanny.

18:32.292 --> 18:34.168
- Hoedown!
- Hootenanny!

18:34.378 --> 18:36.338
- Hoedown!
- Hootenanny!

18:39.800 --> 18:42.719
Thank you. Thank you very much. Thank you.

18:42.802 --> 18:46.972
Oh, and to the owner of a John Deere tractor,
you're parked on top of a pig.

18:47.097 --> 18:49.683
John Deere tractor on top of a pig.

18:50.100 --> 18:53.771
- Sam, can I talk to you?
- Sure. But why aren't you lookin' at me?

18:53.854 --> 18:59.817
Well, that's the thing. I'm no good at talking
to girls. That's why I ran away from you.

18:59.900 --> 19:03.571
You didn't have trouble talkin' to me
when you thought I was a boy.

19:03.654 --> 19:05.656
Yeah, that's true.

19:05.656 --> 19:08.033
- Just pretend I'm a boy.
- OK.

19:08.158 --> 19:11.077
You wanna go down
to the old town bridge and make out?

19:11.161 --> 19:12.745
Yes, sir!

19:12.828 --> 19:16.165
And in the city,
glasses are considered really sexy.

19:16.290 --> 19:17.833
Ooooh.

19:17.958 --> 19:21.170
Dang, I hope her brother
don't already have dibs on her.

19:22.339 --> 19:27.425
- Where's Chris? That criminal's here.
- He's down by the old town bridge.

19:27.550 --> 19:30.761
You know, my brother
is the one he's here to kill.

19:30.886 --> 19:34.306
My daughter would absolutely love you.

19:36.308 --> 19:40.687
You're so cute.
You're like a skinny Garth Brooks.

19:40.770 --> 19:43.815
- Aha! I got you now, Griffin!
- Aaagh!

19:43.898 --> 19:46.401
- Not so fast, buddy!
- Who are you?

19:46.526 --> 19:49.653
You can call me Officer TJ Hooker.

19:49.653 --> 19:52.363
Sheriff Officer TJ Hooker.

19:52.363 --> 19:54.741
And this is my deputy, McMillan and Wife.

19:54.866 --> 20:00.371
I hated TJ Hooker. And I never actually saw
McMillan and Wife, although I was aware of it.

20:00.496 --> 20:02.873
Anyway, you're dead!

20:03.498 --> 20:05.375
Ha! You're mine now, fella!

20:07.878 --> 20:09.046
Aagh! Aagh!

20:09.129 --> 20:13.008
Aargh! Dad! Help! Dad!

20:15.092 --> 20:18.512
- You folks all right?
- Wow, you guys saved our lives.

20:18.637 --> 20:21.556
And after I said
all Southerners have bad teeth

20:21.639 --> 20:25.518
and the gum disease known as gingivitis.

20:25.602 --> 20:30.398
We take care of our own. And as long as
y'all live here, y'all are Southerners too.

20:30.523 --> 20:35.110
- Wow. Thanks.
- It's our pleasure. Sam, I'll see you at home.

20:35.110 --> 20:38.864
I think the lesson here is
it doesn't matter where you're from,

20:38.947 --> 20:41.991
as long as we're all the same religion.

20:43.117 --> 20:47.830
- It was great having you in class, Meg.
- Thanks. I'm really gonna miss everybody.

20:47.913 --> 20:52.292
We didn't have no money for a present,
so we all just spit in a jar.

20:52.417 --> 20:55.420
- I can't believe you're leavin'.
- Me either.

20:55.545 --> 20:58.882
- I'll be sure to write.
- And I'll be sure to learn to read.

20:58.882 --> 21:05.137
Next time I see a dead guy, I'm gonna
poke him twice as hard for both of us.

21:11.267 --> 21:13.561
Ah, it's so nice to be home.

21:13.686 --> 21:16.897
You have 113 new messages.

21:17.023 --> 21:18.690
Oh, my.

21:18.774 --> 21:23.486
Uh, yeah,
I was just wondering... uh... mm-hm...

21:23.486 --> 21:25.780
where the newspaper boy was.

21:26.823 --> 21:31.493
Haven't seen a newspaper in a couple of days.
Wonderin' if you're ever gonna come back.

21:32.453 --> 21:36.914
Guess who.
Sorry to leave you so many messages.

21:37.040 --> 21:41.836
Just lonely here, thinkin' 'bout
the muscly-armed paper boy.

21:41.836 --> 21:46.005
Wishin' he'd bring me some good news.

21:46.089 --> 21:48.175
Where are you?

21:48.300 --> 21:52.887
You're startin' to piss me off,
you little piggly son of a bitch. Call me.

21:52.888 --> 22:53.888
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru